q BT 65.20 771.39 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (Nina nodded. "My mother said -- the key opens what they stole from us.") Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 741.91 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg ("Stole?" the Don asked. "Who stole from my wife?") Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 712.43 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (Nina looked away. "The man she trusted most.") Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 682.95 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.646 Tw (The next morning, the Don took the key to the bank, to a safe-deposit room he had not entered) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 662.54 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.350 Tw (in years. The key turned. The box opened. Inside lay a single thing: a leather diary, worn soft at) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 642.13 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (the edges.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 612.65 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.051 Tw (He opened it, and his hands began to shake. It was her handwriting. His wife's handwriting, after) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 592.24 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (thirty years.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 562.76 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg ("Her handwriting," he whispered. "After thirty years.") Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 533.28 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg ("Read the last page," Nina said.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 503.80 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (He turned to the end. "She wrote a name here," he said.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 474.32 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (And then he read it -- and everything he believed about his wife's death fell apart.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 444.84 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.269 Tw (The diary was written by Elena Cole, the Don's wife, in the last months of her life -- months the) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 424.43 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (Don had never known existed.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 394.95 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.310 Tw (Elena had discovered the theft first. Money was leaving the family accounts -- quietly, a little at) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 374.54 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 1.331 Tw (a time, then all at once. She followed it, and it led her to the one man she would never have) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 354.13 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.554 Tw (suspected: Vincent Marone, the Don's own younger brother, the man who sat at the Don's table) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 333.72 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (every Sunday and called him brother.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 304.24 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 1.252 Tw (When Elena confronted him, Vincent did not deny it. He told her, calmly, that if she spoke a) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 283.83 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (word of it, she would lose everything -- and so would the child she was carrying.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 254.35 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (So Elena did the only thing she could do. She left.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 224.87 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.567 Tw (Vincent staged her death -- a car fire on an empty road, with no body ever found -- and he told) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 204.46 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 1.558 Tw (the Don she had died thirty years ago. He told it so often, and with such grief, that the Don) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 184.05 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.498 Tw (believed it. But the diary proved it was a lie. The fire had been twenty-six years ago, not thirty,) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 163.64 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 1.095 Tw (and Elena had been alive all that time, living under her maiden name in a small coastal town,) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 143.23 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (raising the daughter the Don had never known he had.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 113.75 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 2.174 Tw (She sang the song to Nina every night before bed, so the little girl would never forget her) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 93.35 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.017 Tw (mother. She gave Nina the silver necklace on the night she died -- Nina was seven, and sick with) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 72.94 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (fever herself -- and she pressed the locket into her daughter's hand.) Tj ET Q
