q BT 65.20 771.39 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.558 Tw ("The key opens what they stole from us," she told her. "One day, take it to your father. He will) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 750.98 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (know what to do.") Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 721.50 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 1.727 Tw (Elena died of illness that winter. Her mother, Rosa, raised Nina after her, in the same small) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 701.09 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 1.136 Tw (town, and Nina grew up singing her mother's songs in little caf?s -- until the day she was old) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 680.68 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (enough to walk into the Don's club and sing the one song no one alive should know.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 651.20 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 1.467 Tw (The last page of the diary held the name, written in Elena's own hand: Vincent Marone. The) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 630.79 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 1.064 Tw (man who had emptied the family accounts in the week his sister-in-law was supposed to have) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 610.38 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (died. The man who had stolen a wife, a daughter, and twenty-six years from his own brother.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 580.90 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (That Sunday, Vincent Marone came to the table, as he had every Sunday for thirty years.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 551.42 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 1.085 Tw (The Don did not raise his voice. He laid the diary on the table between them, open at the last) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 531.01 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (page, and he watched his brother's face.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 501.53 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 1.015 Tw (Vincent did not deny it. Men like Vincent never deny it; they only ask what the price will be.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 481.12 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.480 Tw (The Don gave him no price. He told him to leave the city before morning and never come back) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 460.72 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (-- and to know, for the rest of his life, that the brother he stole from had found what he stole.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 431.23 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (Then the Don turned to Nina.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 401.75 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 1.223 Tw (That night, in the club, Nina sang the song once more -- this time with the Don sitting in the) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 381.35 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (front row, listening to his own daughter's voice.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 351.86 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 1.013 Tw ("Your mother wrote that song for you," he told her when it ended. "She sang it to you so you) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 331.46 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.613 Tw (would never forget her. I did not know my own daughter's voice, Nina. That will never happen) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 311.05 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (again. You are home now.") Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 281.57 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.157 Tw (Nina nodded, and for the first time in her life, she took off the silver necklace -- and put it in her) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 261.16 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (father's hand.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 231.68 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.664 Tw (He keeps it still, in the top drawer of his desk -- a reminder that the smallest voice in the room) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 211.27 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (can carry the biggest truth, and that a song is only as lost as the people who remember it.) Tj ET Q
